\code{\link[=print]{print()}}, \code{\link[=summary]{summary()}}, \code{\link[=plot]{plot()}} and \code{\link[pillar:tbl_sum]{pillar::tbl_sum()}} methods are
defined once for \code{tbl_vintage} and inherited by both, so that the two stay
consistent with one another. Only the parts that genuinely depend on the
indexing dimension are dispatched on the child classes, through the
internal generics \code{vintage_labels()}, \code{vintage_value_cols()} and
\code{vintage_detail()}.

Both representations may be stored in either a long or a wide layout, and
the methods below detect which and report accordingly. The layouts, and the
columns each one requires, are specified under "Data contract" in
\code{\link[=validate_vintages]{validate_vintages()}}, which also checks an object against them. Use
